From 21991faccc56dcb98c28e6130267dd6cf98af3b4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Your Name <you@example.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 10:13:40 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] sched: symmetric epoch cohort join window -- the
 pre-formation side admits only formation cuts

The owner's anchor ("created within 5 seconds of the start of the epoch")
reads symmetrically: the window now spans [formation-5s, formation+5s].
The post-formation side keeps the W-series semantics unchanged; the
pre-formation side is cut-only -- a row the formation class-guarded may
join once its class flips into the epoch's, while rows queued at
formation stay mid-arrivals (a DE epoch cannot feed them; admitting one
would hang the drain on its own admission freeze). Formation stamps its
cuts in the new epoch_cut_ vector; the planning-pass scan consumes it.
epoch_cut_joins counter unchanged. Mechanism A -- a queued same-burst
row waiting out a live DECODE epoch's full generation -- is
owner-accepted by design (2026-11-21): pinned, not fixed, by
epoch_same_burst_waits_out_live_decode_epoch_by_design. W6 pins the
reachable pre-formation join (PF epoch, preempted cut replaying
prefill-class) and the window bound on the pre side; W4's header is
replaced with the per-direction flip-reachability matrix.
